# The client announces a packet cap of 512 bytes. The host answers with its own cap in mind, so an
# answer bigger than 512 bytes is refused as frame_too_large, under the id of the request; the
# connection stays up, and the next request is answered.
@proxy frames 512
ping
load_plugin {plugin}
put_graph pass {graphs}/pass.json
plan pass steps
inspect graph pass
ping
